{
  "usage": "Code Health bar for bro, version-controlled with the code. The warning thresholds are bro's ceilings: function cyclomatic complexity <= 9, file mean cyclomatic complexity <= 4, function LoC <= 50 (alert 70), file LoC <= 800 (alert 1000), nesting depth <= 4, bumpy road <= 2 bumps at nesting depth 2, function arguments <= 4, constructor arguments <= 5, duplication >= 10 LoC at 75% similarity. The alert thresholds stay at CodeScene's configured value: the alerts are what the PR integration gates on, and moving them moves the gate for the whole repo — a deliberate wave decision, not a default. The rule weights are listed at their default (1.0) so a CodeScene default change cannot silently move bro's bar either. Keep this list COMPLETE: an omitted threshold falls back to a stricter value, not the default (measured: serve-conductor.ts scored 3.80 without this file and 1.84 with 8 thresholds left out). Keep in sync with the ceilings in the codescene skill.",
